ARM SYSCALLS Overview
=====================
http://arch.eece.maine.edu/ece471/images/a/a5/Lecture_10_ARM_Linux_Systemcalls.pdf



User Defs
=========
arch/arm/include/asm/unistd.h
ARM only pvt syscalls (like cacheflush) are at the bottom of that file.



ARM SYSCALL Handler
===================
* syscalls are handled in arch/arm/kernel/entry-common.s in the vector_swi 
  call
* there are 3 tables in that file (grep for them)
** sys_call_table : Regular Linux syscalls 
** sys_ni_syscall : Default syscall handler
** arm_syscall    : ARM private syscall



Regular Syscalls
================
* arch/arm/kernel/calls.S has the actual syscall functions. 
* sys_mprotect is really mprotect. in mprotect.c that SYSCALL_DEFINE3 
  takes care of the name mangling so no worries



ARM Private Syscalls
====================
* arch/arm/kernel/traps.c arm_syscall handles the private syscalls like
  cacheflush

